489 - Jesus, Lover of My Soul
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 489
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Eb]Jesus, lover [Bb]of my soul,
[Eb]Let me to thy [Bb]bosom [Eb]fly,
While the billows [Bb]near me roll,
[Eb]While the tempest [Bb]still is [Eb]high;
[Eb]Hide me, O my [Ab]Savior, [Eb]hide!
Till the storm of [Ab]life is [Eb]past;
Safe into the [Bb]haven guide,
[Eb]O receive my [Bb]soul at [Eb]last!

Verse 2:
[Eb]Other refuge [Bb]has I none,
[Eb]Hangs my [Bb]helpless soul [Eb]on thee;
[Bb]Leave O leave me not alone!
[Eb]Still [Bb]support and [Eb]comfort me;
[Eb]All my [Ab]trust on [Eb]Thee is stayed,
[Ab]All my help [Eb]from Thee I bring;
[Bb]Cover my defenseless head
[Eb]With the [Bb]shadow of [Eb]Thy wing.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Thou, O Christ, [Bb]all I want,
[Eb]More than [Bb]all in [Eb]Thee I find;
[Bb]Raise the fallen, cheer the faint,
[Eb]Heal the [Bb]sick, and [Eb]lead the blind.
[Eb]Just and [Ab]holy is [Eb]Thy name,
[Ab]I am [Eb]all unrighteousness;
[Bb]Vile and full of sin I am;
[Eb]Thou art [Bb]full of [Eb]truth and grace.

Verse 4:
[Eb]Plenteous grace with [Bb]Thee is found-
[Eb]Grace to [Bb]pardon all [Eb]my sin;
[Bb]Let the healing streams abound,
[Eb]Make and [Bb]keep me [Eb]pure within;
[Eb]Thou of [Ab]life the [Eb]Fountain art,
[Ab]Freely let me [Eb]take of Thee;
[Bb]Spring Thou up within my heart,
[Eb]Rise [Bb]to [Eb]all eternity.
